# This stack is built and run on Linux/WSL (Docker, shell scripts), so every
# text file is normalized to LF in the repo and checked out as LF regardless of
# the cloner's OS or core.autocrlf setting. Git still auto-detects binaries and
# leaves them byte-for-byte untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are LF-only: CRLF makes the kernel fail to find the interpreter.
*.sh text eol=lf
